class.description:
[PckPackageServer] is the one place for everything about [code].pck[/code] files. It opens a pack and lists its content without mounting it ([method open]), reads and verifies single files, builds a new pack from a [PckPackage] ([method build]), writes the files of a pack into a folder ([method extract]), mounts and unmounts packs, and tells which pack provides a [code]res://[/code] file ([method get_pack_of]). Mods, DLC, patches and level editors use it to inspect and change packs at runtime.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# Inspect a pack without mounting it.
var package := PckPackageServer.open("user://mods/level_pack.pck")
for entry in package.get_entries():
	print(entry.path, " ", entry.size)
print(PckPackageServer.read_file(package, "res://levels/readme.txt").get_string_from_utf8())

# Mount it, use it, unmount it.
PckPackageServer.mount("user://mods/level_pack.pck")
print(PckPackageServer.get_pack_of("res://levels/readme.txt")) # user://mods/level_pack.pck
PckPackageServer.unmount("user://mods/level_pack.pck")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// Inspect a pack without mounting it.
PckPackage package = PckPackageServer.Open("user://mods/level_pack.pck");
foreach (Godot.Collections.Dictionary entry in package.GetEntries())
{
    GD.Print(entry["path"], " ", entry["size"]);
}
GD.Print(PckPackageServer.ReadFile(package, "res://levels/readme.txt").GetStringFromUtf8());

// Mount it, use it, unmount it.
PckPackageServer.Mount("user://mods/level_pack.pck");
GD.Print(PckPackageServer.GetPackOf("res://levels/readme.txt")); // user://mods/level_pack.pck
PckPackageServer.Unmount("user://mods/level_pack.pck");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Pack paths can use any path prefix registered with [PathPrefixServer], for example [code]exec://mods/a.pck[/code].
[b]Encryption keys:[/b] a key is a [String] of 64 hexadecimal characters (256 bits), as used by [PCKPacker]. An empty key means the script encryption key compiled into the engine.
[b]Platforms:[/b] all methods work on every platform. On Android, iOS and the Web, packs can only be written to [code]user://[/code]. On the Web, packs are read from the main pack or from [code]user://[/code] (IndexedDB); files written there are persisted asynchronously.

method.description:
Writes the files of [param package] into the folder [param target_dir], keeping their paths: [code]res://levels/a.tscn[/code] becomes [code]target_dir/levels/a.tscn[/code]. Missing folders are created. The pack does not need to be mounted. Returns a [PckExtractResult] that lists the written, skipped, renamed and not editable files, the dropped UIDs and the errors. [signal extract_progress] is emitted after each file.
[param paths] selects the files to extract; an empty array extracts all files. Each entry is a file path, a folder (every file below it, for example [code]"res://levels/"[/code]) or a pattern with [code]*[/code] and [code]?[/code] (see [method String.match]), with or without [code]res://[/code]. The [code].import[/code] and [code].uid[/code] files of a selected file are selected with it.
[param policy] decides what happens to files that already exist in [param target_dir]: they are skipped ([constant EXTRACT_SKIP]), overwritten ([constant EXTRACT_OVERWRITE]) or the file is written under a free name like [code]a_2.tscn[/code] ([constant EXTRACT_RENAME]). [code].import[/code] and [code].uid[/code] files follow the file they belong to: [code]icon.png.import[/code] is skipped, overwritten or renamed to [code]icon_2.png.import[/code] together with [code]icon.png[/code].
With [param skip_engine_files], files that can't be used as sources are left out: everything below [code].godot/[/code], [code].import[/code] and [code].uid[/code] files whose source file is not extracted, removal entries, and [code]project.binary[/code], [code].remap[/code] files and delta patches, which are listed in [member PckExtractResult.not_editable]. Exported packs contain imported and converted files instead of the sources, so for them extracting is a best-effort copy of the data; packs built from a [PckPackage] description with source files are extracted completely.
[b]UIDs:[/b] a UID from a [code].uid[/code] file, from the [code]uid="…"[/code] attribute of a [code].tscn[/code] or [code].tres[/code] header, from an [code].import[/code] file or from a binary [code].scn[/code]/[code].res[/code] file is kept if no other file uses it, and is registered with [ResourceUID] at once, so [code]uid://[/code] paths of the extracted files work before the next editor scan. A UID that already belongs to another file is dropped and listed in [member PckExtractResult.dropped_uids]: the [code].uid[/code] file is not written, the attribute is removed from text resources and [code].import[/code] files (the editor assigns a new UID on the next scan), and binary resources get a new UID.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var package := PckPackageServer.open("user://downloads/mod.pck")
var result := PckPackageServer.extract(package, "user://mods/my_mod", [], PckPackageServer.EXTRACT_OVERWRITE)
if not result.is_ok():
    push_error("\n".join(result.errors))
print("%d files written" % result.written.size())
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
PckPackage package = PckPackageServer.Open("user://downloads/mod.pck");
PckExtractResult result = PckPackageServer.Extract(package, "user://mods/my_mod", [], PckPackageServer.ExtractPolicy.Overwrite);
if (!result.IsOk())
{
    GD.PushError(string.Join("\n", result.Errors));
}
GD.Print($"{result.Written.Length} files written");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Platforms:[/b] works on every platform. [code]res://[/code] is writable only in the editor; exported games, Android and iOS extract into [code]user://[/code]. On the Web, files in [code]user://[/code] are persisted to IndexedDB asynchronously; one file at a time is held in memory.
